1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,920
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:12,762
<i>-Careful.</i>
<i>-Hey!</i>

3
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:14,723
[Arnaldo] <i>I don't like what</i>
<i>you did earlier.</i>

4
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:16,725
[Diego] <i>If you always</i>
<i>got what you wanted back then,</i>

5
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>it won't happen this time.</i>

6
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>Ivy doesn't like you.</i>

7
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:20,729
-[Ivy screams]
-<i>Oh!</i>

8
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:22,021
[Ivy] <i>What were you doing?!</i>

9
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:24,733
<i>-How dare you peep on me!</i>
<i>-I said I'm sorry!</i>

10
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,985
[Loring] <i>He had only one best friend,</i>

11
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:30,238
<i>and she was his one and only true love.</i>

12
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,407
<i>What's her name, Diego?</i>

13
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:35,618
<i>Lily. Her name is Lily.</i>

14
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:39,164
<i>I have here an old draft,</i>
<i>the deed of donation from 1958,</i>

15
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:42,125
<i>confirming that the land</i>
<i>was donated to the farmers.</i>

16
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:44,711
[crowd clamoring]

17
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:46,087
<i>So, you got what you wanted.</i>

18
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,589
<i>When do I get my end of the bargain?</i>

19
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:50,049
<i>Miss Ivy was concerned.</i>

20
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,843
<i>All right, Nanny. I'll talk to Miss Aguas.</i>

21
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:52,969
<i>You're different.</i>

22
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,889
<i>You've got the perfect</i>
<i>characteristics of a first lady.</i>

23
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,599
<i>My first lady.</i>

24
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:58,808
[Diego] <i>Miss Aguas, wait!</i>

25
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:03,438
<i>How dare you go against your own family?</i>

26
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:06,900
<i>If you pull this stunt again,</i>
<i>Diego, you will answer to me.</i>

27
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,610
<i>You will answer to me!</i>

28
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:11,571
[Raul] <i>Someday I'll be</i>
<i>as powerful as them.</i>

29
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:14,783
<i>And when that happens, I'll leave Emilia.</i>

30
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,701
<i>And I'll choose you, Camia.</i>

31
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,703
[Carlotta] <i>Diego is a good man.</i>

32
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:20,705
<i>You're fighting for the same thing.</i>

33
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>It isn't wrong to open</i>
<i>your heart to someone.</i>

34
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:27,295
<i>I shouldn't feel this way about</i>
<i>you because you're the enemy.</i>

35
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>But why can't I get you off my mind?</i>

36
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:32,509
[Ivy] Joan, how are the contracts?

37
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:34,427
-Okay, very good.
-Ivy.

38
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:36,513
Ivy, where are you going?

39
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:40,809
I have to go to Manila
to meet with a new investor.

40
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:43,812
Why don't you rest first?

41
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,063
I know you're stressed out

42
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,190
with everything that's happening here.

43
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:51,402
Thank you for your concern,
but I can handle myself.

44
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:54,239
You know I have to attend to my business.

45
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:56,157
I'll be back as soon as I can.

46
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,784
Please take care.

47
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,340
What happened?

48
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,466
I'll go check, ma'am.

49
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,387
Joan, did we run out of working vans?

50
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:19,889
I'm sorry, Miss Ivy.

51
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:31,317
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

52
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,531
[Diego] Sir, what happened?

53
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,283
We have a flat tire, sir.

54
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,410
Let me help you.

55
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:55,800
That's the flat tire, sir.

56
00:02:58,803 --> 00:03:00,847
I think you drove over a nail.

57
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:02,348
Do you have tools with you?

58
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,809
-Yes, sir.
-Can you go get them, please?

59
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,899
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary
continues playing]

60
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:26,706
Mr. Torillo.

61
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:31,002
Miss Aguas, so this is your car.

62
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:34,714
Yes. It's a company car.

63
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:37,717
I'm going back to Manila
for a business meeting.

64
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:45,767
Thank you for letting us
hold the dialogue.

65
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:49,646
I was supposed to tell you that
when I saw you with Arnaldo.

66
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,775
Sorry for ruining your moment.

67
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,779
Nothing's going on
between your brother and I.

68
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:03,368
I mean, Mr. Mayor.

69
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:08,581
I'll just help your driver.

70
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,083
-Mr. Torillo.
-Sir.

71
00:04:14,545 --> 00:04:15,797
Thank you.

72
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:20,301
Even though we're on different sides…

73
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,387
you're still willing to help me out.

74
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:25,807
Also, I'm thankful…

75
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:32,647
that you aren't forcing me
out of this town.

76
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:36,025
Maybe…

77
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:40,488
it's time we called a truce between us.

78
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:44,409
Since you're helping me…

79
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:49,122
maybe this can be
the start of our friendship.

80
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:03,845
Okay, Miss Aguas.

81
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:09,600
You can call me Ivy.

82
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,191
Diego.

83
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:23,865
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

84
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:47,805
I've got to hand it to you Ardientes.

85
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:51,225
Your charity events are always successful.

86
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,727
Of course, Senator.

87
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:56,481
This is the reason we're
so close to our constituents.

88
00:05:56,773 --> 00:06:00,193
By the way, where is Raul?

89
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:01,736
[chuckles softly]

90
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:04,697
He's taking care of something
for our business.

91
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,992
By the way, our EPZ project
starts next week.

92
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:09,702
Okay.

93
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:12,663
But I heard your son, Diego,
tried to stop the project.

94
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:16,626
Sorry to say, but if you can't
control your son,

95
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,338
what more the people of Ardiente?

96
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,803
Oh, I think we have a
very interesting guest

97
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:28,554
behind you, Emilia.

98
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,392
-Hi, Senator.
-Raul.

99
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:34,602
Hello.

100
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:39,232
Emilia, I'm sorry I'm late.

101
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:42,068
For you.

102
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,238
What a pleasant surprise.

103
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,657
Well, shall we have something to eat?

104
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:50,368
Thank you.

105
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:02,922
Thank you.

106
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:07,885
Miss Aguas.

107
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,807
-Ivy.
-[both chuckle]

108
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,477
Thank you, Diego.

109
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,647
Sorry it's not much. But it tastes good.

110
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:24,527
[mellow music plays]

111
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:33,744
This is your favorite, huh?

112
00:07:34,912 --> 00:07:35,997
How did you know?

113
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:41,961
Well, Miss Loring sells these, right?

114
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,590
Yes, ever since I was a kid.

115
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,633
It's my best friend's favorite, too.

116
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:53,723
Your best friend,

117
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,976
she's the one
we talked about before, right?

118
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:59,103
The one who helped you lose weight

119
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,606
because you were chubby…

120
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,274
[snickers]

121
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:04,400
…back then.

122
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:08,196
That wasn't the only thing she taught me.

123
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:10,740
She also taught me how
to stand up for myself,

124
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:12,325
to know my worth.

125
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:14,160
You know…

126
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,204
I tried looking for her…

127
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:18,748
but couldn't find her.

128
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,792
Sometimes, I think about how she's doing.

129
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:23,794
I wonder what she looks like.

130
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,549
I don't even know if she's alive.

131
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:33,763
I don't know why she just disappeared.

132
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,806
She never came back.

133
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:54,992
Diego.

134
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:56,577
Yeah?

135
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:01,541
Diego, that girl…

136
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:06,796
[Joan] Ma'am!

137
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,798
Miss Ivy, the car's ready now.

138
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,049
We can go now.

139
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:13,553
Let's go.

140
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:16,222
Hurry up, please.

141
00:09:18,558 --> 00:09:20,393
I'll just take this with me, Diego.

142
00:09:20,476 --> 00:09:21,978
I really have to go.

143
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:23,479
Make sure you eat it, okay?

144
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:25,439
Take care, Ivy. Be safe!

145
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:26,524
Take care, sir.

146
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:28,818
-Take care.
-Thank you.

147
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,036
[engine turns over]

148
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,799
Emilia, wait.

149
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,342
Emilia.

150
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,515
What's wrong with you?

151
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,601
How many times do you have to lie?

152
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,144
I'm so tired of it.

153
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:05,521
How many families do I have to kill?

154
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,608
We celebrate that day only once a year,

155
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:11,152
when I remember that you loved me once,

156
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:12,612
but you still can't give me that.

157
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:36,427
Looks like you failed
to impress Senator, Mom.

158
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:40,681
You know, this is all your fault.

159
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,558
If you didn't force me to have a dialogue

160
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,809
with those wretched farmers,

161
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,936
they wouldn't see any flaws
with my project.

162
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:48,314
Well, I think Ivy has a point.

163
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,691
We should befriend the people,

164
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:52,276
not push them away.

165
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,863
How do you expect me to trust your plans,

166
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:59,867
when all you really want
is to get inside Ivy's pants?

167
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:01,786
You know what?

168
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:03,204
You're stupid.

169
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:06,374
I'm stupid? Really?

170
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:07,917
Why don't you look at yourself?

171
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:11,087
Until now, you're being stupid for Dad…

172
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:15,049
who doesn't even know
what's happening here.

173
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:17,635
Just like your other good-for-nothing son.

174
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:23,474
You know, I can't help but think
that if Grandpa were here…

175
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:27,686
he wouldn't let this slide.

176
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,690
We wouldn't be having these problems.

177
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,988
Well, I'm the one here.

178
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:43,411
And I'm more than capable
of solving these problems.

179
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,093
Good morning.

180
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:00,719
Is Mr. Fernan there?

181
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,096
Is he the leader of the cooperative?

182
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,597
We have to talk to him.

183
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:07,351
[tense music playing]

184
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:10,271
Mom.

185
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:12,773
What did you do?

186
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:17,736
Arnaldo, I don't want any stress.

187
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,947
So, I did what I had to do.

188
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:21,824
I taught them a lesson.

189
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:29,790
[phone rings]

190
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:32,376
Jepoy.

191
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:36,464
What?! I'll be there.

192
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:40,301
Mister, take me to the cooperative. Hurry.

193
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:42,386
Why is this happening?

194
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:44,221
The governor promised

195
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,682
that she wouldn't evict us
from this land anymore.

196
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,601
Why are you doing this all of a sudden?

197
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,644
And is this even legal?
Do you have papers?

198
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,104
Are you police officers?

199
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,690
The word of the Ardientes is the law here.

200
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,609
Our job is to implement them,

201
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,777
even if it means
evicting you from this land.

202
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,696
If you don't give us a hard time,

203
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:01,864
then no one will get hurt.

204
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:03,407
But if you do,

205
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,159
then you'll be sorry.

206
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:07,578
-That's not what we agreed on.
-No!

207
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:09,997
-Come on, let's talk this out.
-We won't leave.

208
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:13,292
You'll have to kill us first
before you can throw us out.

209
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,675
-Where are you going?
-Where else?

210
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:23,802
I'll handle it.
I'm the head of this project.

211
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:29,433
Okay, I'm sure our private army
needs all the help they can get.

212
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:30,684
Just be careful.

213
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:34,188
You know you'll be evicting a
lot of farmers from that place.

214
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,273
And make sure that
after everything is over,

215
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:38,651
I'll never see their faces again.

216
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:40,486
You take care, okay?

217
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:51,580
Who's that?

218
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,750
-[tense music plays]
-It's Miss Aguas.

219
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:55,834
Diego.

220
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,295
Diego, it's Miss Ivy.
What's she doing here?

221
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:01,507
She's showing her true colors.

222
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:04,301
[Pandoy] But I thought--

223
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,095
We were wrong about her.

224
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,013
She just tricked us.

225
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:10,224
What's happening here?

226
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,976
Ma'am, the governor wants them to leave.

227
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:15,729
Don't tell me you didn't know.

228
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:18,816
Diego, I didn't!

229
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:21,610
Believe it or not, I didn't know.

230
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:24,321
Miss Ivy, the governor
wants us out of this place.

231
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:25,698
-Yeah.
-That's true.

232
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:26,782
What?!

233
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:29,618
Diego.

234
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,247
[tense music intensifies]

235
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:52,725
-She's evicting you?
-Yes.

236
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:54,059
-Ivy.
-Diego.

237
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:57,438
Mr. Mayor, it didn't have to come to this.

238
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,772
Why is this happening?

239
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:00,733
You can't plead their case anymore, Ivy.

240
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:02,985
They have to leave,
whether you like it or not.

241
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:06,822
No. Do something about it.

242
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,454
Diego, there's nothing we can do.

243
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:14,496
No, Nanny.

244
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,999
As long as we're alive, we'll fight back.

245
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:18,000
That's right!

246
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,710
-Let's go, Nanny.
-We're going to fight!

247
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:22,338
Everyone, let's band together!

248
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:23,797
Let's go, everyone.

249
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:26,258
You will never have this land!

250
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:28,093
-This land is ours!
-You can't make us leave!

251
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,554
-We're going to fight!
-You won't take this from us!

252
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,098
[indistinct shouting]

253
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:34,475
We will not leave!

254
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:36,727
-Get out of here!
-We're going to fight!

255
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,312
Arnaldo, do something.

256
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:42,316
[indistinct shouting]

257
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,612
This land is ours!

258
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:47,780
Miss Aguas, let's go.

259
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,865
[indistinct shouting]

260
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:51,700
Come on!

261
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:52,576
-Mr. Mayor.
-Let them be.

262
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,954
Do something. Make them stop.

263
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:56,455
Go on. Make them disperse.

264
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,416
Butchoy!

265
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,502
Let's go. Let's go.

266
00:16:01,585 --> 00:16:02,586
Butchoy.

267
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:04,713
-Wait!
-Miss Aguas!

268
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:06,090
-Butchoy!
-Miss Aguas!

269
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,174
-Butchoy.
-Stop!

270
00:16:08,425 --> 00:16:09,718
Don't cry, Butchoy.

271
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:10,803
Mr. Mayor, make them stop!

272
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:13,389
There's an innocent child here!

273
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:17,017
[tense music playing]

274
00:16:17,184 --> 00:16:18,811
Miss Aguas, you should get out of here.

275
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,437
You need to go!

276
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:22,773
Take Butchoy and go!

277
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,734
Madrigal, go get her. Make it quick.

278
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:29,905
-You need to go.
-Make them disperse.

279
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,907
-You have to leave. Go.
-Calm down! Pandoy!

280
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:34,493
-Hey! Hey!
-Stop!

281
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:36,704
[Ivy] Don't cry, Butchoy. Don't cry.

282
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:38,414
-Let's go
-But the kid--

283
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:40,708
-Let's go!
-Butchoy!

284
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:43,836
[clamoring]

285
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,421
Hold on! Stop!

286
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:46,714
Hey, get your hands off them!

287
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:47,548
-Pandoy!
-Stop it!

288
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:49,383
-Wait!
-Let's go.

289
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,014
Mr. Mayor, have pity on your brother.

290
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,807
Hey! Stop! Wait!

291
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,809
[Diego] I said let her go!

292
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:02,021
There's nothing we can do. He wanted that.

293
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:03,647
Wait! Wait!

294
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:05,607
[Loring screams]

295
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,864
[tense music continues playing]

296
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:37,681
-Let her go! Wait!
-[Loring] Diego!

297
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:38,724
Stop!

298
00:17:38,807 --> 00:17:39,725
-Get in!
-Let them go!

299
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:42,352
Arnaldo! Make them stop! Wait!

300
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:44,063
-[Loring] Diego!
-Stop!

301
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:45,397
Ouch!

302
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:47,775
Bastards!

303
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:48,942
Stop!

304
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,778
-Close the door!
-[Loring] Diego!

305
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:52,821
Hold on. Hold on.

306
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,573
Stop! This is wrong!

307
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:55,699
-Come on. Go.
-Diego!

308
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,785
-[man] Diego!
-Hold on!

309
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:58,952
Get out of here!

310
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,120
Mayor! Mayor!

311
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:02,623
Now what, Diego?

312
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:04,917
Are you going to punch me?

313
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:06,877
Then do it!

314
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:08,796
Hit me!

315
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:11,632
You don't have it in you.

316
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,384
[screams]

317
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,928
Why did it have to be like this?!

318
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:18,138
Tell me, Arnaldo!

319
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:20,182
Why can't you all understand?!

320
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:23,268
This is for everyone!
This is for the town!

321
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:24,311
Lies!

322
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,355
You know that's a lie!

323
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:30,109
It hasn't been 30 days
since you gave us the notice!

324
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,318
You don't have a court order,

325
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:32,903
because we all know

326
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:34,655
this didn't go through due process.

327
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,658
The farmers will file an appeal!

328
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:40,869
And while the Supreme Court
hasn't made its final decision,

329
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,080
then you can't force us off this land.

330
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:45,749
You can't kick the farmers out!

331
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:48,794
[tense music intensifies]

332
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:51,797
Well?! Say something!

333
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:54,716
What now?!

334
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:56,510
Release him.

335
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:57,845
Break it off, everyone.

336
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,597
All right. Let them go.

337
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,641
But remember this.

338
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:05,227
We wouldn't have resorted to violence

339
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:07,646
if it weren't for your stubbornness!

340
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:09,731
Everything that happened today
is your fault!

341
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:13,777
It's your fault.

342
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,362
[camera clicks]

343
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:18,615
Let's go.

344
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:22,786
[camera clicks]

345
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,339
-Move!
-Diego!

346
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:36,383
-Wait!
-Diego!

347
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:38,010
-Diego!
-Stop! Arnaldo!

348
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:39,094
-Diego!
-Diego!

349
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:40,804
-Arnaldo!
-Diego!

350
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,639
-Move out!
-Nanny!

351
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,729
-Diego!
-Let's move!

352
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:50,772
-[engine revs]
-Diego!

353
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:58,739
Raul! Aren't you going out?

354
00:20:00,365 --> 00:20:03,660
When I'm not here, you get mad.

355
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:06,163
And now that I'm here,
you tell me to leave!

356
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:09,583
I'm not leaving because I'm
waiting for your son, Arnaldo!

357
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:12,753
Yes? I heard my name.

358
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:15,214
Arnaldo, what did you do?

359
00:20:15,339 --> 00:20:17,132
Why did you let Diego get beaten up?

360
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,718
-Diego? Well, he asked for it.
-He asked for it?

361
00:20:19,801 --> 00:20:21,637
This is your brother we're talking about.

362
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,848
Raul, can you calm down?

363
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:28,727
I allowed that to happen
to teach him a lesson.

364
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:30,896
It's not as if his life was in any danger.

365
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:33,315
What kind of answer is that, Emilia?

366
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:35,025
You let them hurt Diego?

367
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:38,820
What kind of family is this?

368
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,739
We're not done yet, Arnaldo.

369
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:44,368
Oh, Ivy, I'm sorry
you had to witness that.

370
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:46,703
My husband isn't politically savvy,

371
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:48,872
so I wasn't able to teach him any manners.

372
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:53,085
I guess that's why I was
so patient with those farmers.

373
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:56,797
You know, we live in a house
full of parasites.

374
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,174
But you're not included, Arnaldo.

375
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:03,804
Anyway, the operation stopped
because of what happened.

376
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,014
But once we demolish the houses,

377
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,684
they won't have any choice but
to live in the relocation site.

378
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:12,562
I have to go to my office. Excuse me.

379
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:18,819
Will the project still push through?

380
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,696
Yes, of course.

381
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,906
We're Ardientes. We get what we want.

382
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:34,501
You can't do this to us.

383
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:36,837
We're just fighting for our rights!

384
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:39,256
-Ramon, calm down!
-He's right.

385
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,717
I can't trust those Ardientes anymore.

386
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:46,805
Especially after treating us
like animals today!

387
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:51,518
Let's talk about this peacefully.

388
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:55,689
We're all residents of Ardiente…

389
00:21:56,231 --> 00:22:01,862
so, please, just give us
a little consideration.

390
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:04,740
Don't tell us that.

391
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:06,700
Tell that to the mayor,

392
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:08,702
or maybe, the governor,

393
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:11,496
or maybe, Miss Ivy Aguas.

394
00:22:12,539 --> 00:22:14,207
[tense music plays]

395
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:18,003
Actually, that's what I wanted
to make sure of.

396
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:21,423
Emilia, is this what you really want?

397
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:23,884
For the people you govern

398
00:22:24,009 --> 00:22:27,262
to lose their homes and their livelihood?

399
00:22:27,345 --> 00:22:28,805
This isn't right.

400
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:29,848
Okay, sure.

401
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:32,893
You'll relocate them elsewhere.

402
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:36,229
But that's far from the life they know.

403
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,732
Emilia, have you thought of that?

404
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:46,156
I thought Miss Ivy asked them to stop.

405
00:22:46,573 --> 00:22:49,618
She looked so surprised
when she saw what was happening.

406
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:51,787
[Loring] I'm so confused.

407
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:54,331
Is she telling the truth or not?

408
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:58,710
Fine, I want to invest here
and partner up with you,

409
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:01,671
but, Emilia, this is not what I wanted.

410
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:03,715
[sighs]

411
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:05,842
Ivy, you know, you surprised me.

412
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:08,178
You know what? We should celebrate.

413
00:23:08,261 --> 00:23:10,680
I brought out my most expensive
bottle of wine.

414
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:13,058
[sighs]

415
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:17,521
Victory is sweet when
you get what you want.

416
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:19,898
But it is sweeter…

417
00:23:20,774 --> 00:23:23,902
if you get it without hurting anyone.

418
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:29,157
Emilia, you even let your son get hurt.

419
00:23:30,158 --> 00:23:31,701
He went against me.

420
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:33,453
He went against us.

421
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:34,871
That's why I had to do that.

422
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:37,707
Otherwise, your investment
would go down the drain.

423
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:39,626
And I don't want that to happen.

424
00:23:43,171 --> 00:23:47,008
Hmm… Unless you've switched sides.

425
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:52,389
[tense music intensifies]

426
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:55,892
Excuse me.

427
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,523
[Jepoy] What's his name?

428
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,817
The governor's really scary.

429
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:05,152
Imagine that?

430
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:07,487
She kicked those farmers off their land.

431
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:10,782
Well, the governor already
told them to move ahead of time.

432
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:12,701
It's those farmers' fault.

433
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:14,077
They overstayed their welcome.

434
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,621
What the Ardientes did was right.

435
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:18,290
I guess.

436
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:22,794
But what if those farmers
get back at them?

437
00:24:23,461 --> 00:24:25,046
That's impossible.

438
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:26,631
As if they'd have the guts to do that.

439
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:30,135
Thing is, no matter
how obedient sheep may be,

440
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:33,763
when their patience runs out,
they can turn into wolves.

441
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:36,266
They might come for the Ardientes…

442
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:39,519
or even their investor, Ivy Aguas.

443
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:43,440
That's going to make our jobs
as bodyguards harder.

444
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,150
That's more work for us.

445
00:24:45,233 --> 00:24:46,610
What do you think, Jepoy?

446
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:50,614
Farmers? You think they stand
a chance against us?

447
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:53,074
Drink your coffee.

448
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:55,827
-You're just hungry.
-[phone vibrates]

449
00:24:58,705 --> 00:25:00,790
MEET ME AT THE PARKING LOT

450
00:25:03,793 --> 00:25:04,794
Anyway, see you guys later.

451
00:25:05,795 --> 00:25:06,796
Sure.

452
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,305
[phone rings]

453
00:25:17,599 --> 00:25:18,600
Ivy?

454
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:20,185
Jepoy, I want you to check on Diego.

455
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,770
<i>Make sure he's all right.</i>

456
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:23,230
Diego?

457
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:26,691
Yes, check on Diego,
Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy.

458
00:25:26,775 --> 00:25:28,068
<i>Everyone at the cooperative.</i>

459
00:25:28,151 --> 00:25:30,320
I want you to make sure they're okay.

460
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:33,782
Jepoy, I can't leave
because I'm with Emilia.

461
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:36,368
I know she's getting suspicious.

462
00:25:36,993 --> 00:25:38,662
She's starting to doubt me.

463
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:42,749
So, please, do this for me.

464
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:43,833
Okay?

465
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:49,839
Ivy?

466
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:55,387
What are you doing here?

467
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:57,180
I had to take a call.

468
00:25:57,430 --> 00:25:58,598
I know, I heard.

469
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:00,183
Who were you talking to?

470
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:11,152
I was talking to Nanny Carlotta.

471
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:12,779
I just gave her some instructions.

472
00:26:13,196 --> 00:26:14,155
Why?

473
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:16,992
Is there anything you wanna talk about?

474
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:20,078
Are you following me, Emilia?

475
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:21,663
No!

476
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:24,374
You just look agitated.

477
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:28,211
And I'm sure you've heard
about the dispersal.

478
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,714
I just wanna make sure
that it's business as usual.

479
00:26:30,797 --> 00:26:31,923
That it's still on.

480
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,271
Isn't that Mr. Diego Ardiente?

481
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:48,773
[tires screech]

482
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:53,361
Mr. Diego, what's the problem?

483
00:26:54,654 --> 00:26:55,739
Let them go!

484
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:59,367
Aren't you scared, Mr. Diego?

485
00:26:59,576 --> 00:27:00,744
We're armed.

486
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:03,246
-And you know…
-Hey, look, it's Diego!

487
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:05,540
…we can't follow your orders.

488
00:27:05,623 --> 00:27:07,751
Why, is the governor here? Or the mayor?

489
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:10,962
You're my family's private army.
And I'm an Ardiente!

490
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:12,714
-Let's get down.
-Come on.

491
00:27:12,797 --> 00:27:14,341
-Dad! Dad!
-Hey!

492
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:16,760
-Hey, Loring.
-Diego, Diego.

493
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,636
Hey, who said you could get down?

494
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:20,013
-Hey!
-Let me go!

495
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:22,223
Diego!

496
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:24,309
You have no right to hurt them!

497
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:25,727
We'll see!

498
00:27:25,810 --> 00:27:26,686
-Hold on!
-Please! Don't!

499
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:28,938
Go on, shoot! Shoot me!

500
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:32,692
Come on! Shoot me!

501
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:35,820
Say goodbye to your protectors
if something bad happens to me!

502
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:41,785
I know you're just following orders…

503
00:27:42,535 --> 00:27:45,789
but that's no reason
to act like criminals!

504
00:27:46,247 --> 00:27:47,207
Everyone!

505
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:48,708
-Yeah?
-Come with me.

506
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:50,043
-Yes.
-Okay.

507
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:51,753
-All right, Diego.
-Nanny, Uncle, let's go.

508
00:27:51,836 --> 00:27:54,297
-Thank you, Diego.
-Dad! Dad!

509
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:55,382
Dad!

510
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:03,807
[people clamoring]

511
00:28:06,851 --> 00:28:07,977
[Emilia] <i>No, no, no.</i>

512
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:10,021
<i>Why was the press there?</i>

513
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:12,774
<i>Now, I have to clean it up.</i>

514
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:14,275
<i>News blackout.</i>

515
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:17,070
<i>These rookies do nothing</i>
<i>but mess things up.</i>

516
00:28:17,153 --> 00:28:18,196
<i>Who am I?</i>

517
00:28:18,279 --> 00:28:20,323
<i>Cinderella who has to mop up their mess?</i>

518
00:28:21,574 --> 00:28:23,201
<i>I'm lucky I'm good at it.</i>

519
00:28:26,871 --> 00:28:28,915
[Loring] Oh, my goodness.

520
00:28:28,998 --> 00:28:30,667
What happened here?

521
00:28:33,628 --> 00:28:35,171
They really won't stop.

522
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:38,425
They'll do everything to make us give up.

523
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:40,760
So, everyone…

524
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:43,638
we have to be strong and brave.

525
00:28:43,930 --> 00:28:48,268
Let's show them that whatever
happens, we stand united.

526
00:28:55,275 --> 00:28:56,693
-Diego.
-Careful.

527
00:28:56,776 --> 00:28:57,777
Dad.

528
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:05,368
[Ivy] Jepoy.

529
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:07,245
Jepoy, what's the update on Diego?

530
00:29:07,328 --> 00:29:08,329
<i>I passed by the co-op.</i>

531
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:10,248
I saw Diego and the farmers there.

532
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:13,585
You did?

533
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:15,628
Jepoy, thank you.

534
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:16,880
That's good to know.

535
00:29:17,464 --> 00:29:18,506
Ivy.

536
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:20,508
I just want to ask something.

537
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:23,762
What's going on between--

538
00:29:27,098 --> 00:29:29,350
Forget it. Never mind.

539
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:32,395
Anyway, take care, okay?

540
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,023
And thanks again.

541
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:46,951
You really love everyone here, don't you?

542
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:49,120
I do, Dad.

543
00:29:49,954 --> 00:29:51,414
They're like family to me.

544
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:55,126
But that's not the reason
I'm helping them.

545
00:29:56,377 --> 00:29:57,796
Dad, they're in the right.

546
00:29:58,421 --> 00:30:00,131
If no one will stand up for them,

547
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:02,592
all this injustice won't stop.

548
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:08,389
I know. But I also want to remind you

549
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:12,602
that you're not just dealing
with random people.

550
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:14,771
You're dealing with your mom and brother.

551
00:30:16,147 --> 00:30:18,149
I know, Dad. But nothing will change

552
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:20,735
if no one stands up for what's right.

553
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:27,909
Son, I'm proud of you.

554
00:30:28,535 --> 00:30:30,829
Because you didn't
listen to all the things

555
00:30:30,912 --> 00:30:32,789
your grandfather
and mother have been spouting.

556
00:30:33,498 --> 00:30:35,124
Instead, you chose to believe in yourself.

557
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:37,627
It's good that you're true
to your own principles.

558
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:45,802
I just hope one day, I can do the same.

559
00:30:46,761 --> 00:30:48,221
I want to be like you.

560
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:51,224
I want to be brave
and stand up for myself.

561
00:30:58,314 --> 00:31:01,109
-Ma'am, good morning.
-Let me get that.

562
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:02,235
Okay, ma'am.

563
00:31:05,905 --> 00:31:06,948
Ivy.

564
00:31:07,782 --> 00:31:09,909
Isn't that too much?

565
00:31:10,326 --> 00:31:12,704
To be honest, this
isn't even enough to pay

566
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:16,124
for all the pain I've caused.

567
00:31:16,791 --> 00:31:17,959
Nowhere near enough.

568
00:31:18,167 --> 00:31:20,795
But how will you give it to them?

569
00:31:21,796 --> 00:31:22,797
Through Diego.

570
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:26,718
I'll tell him that it's just
a small amount

571
00:31:26,801 --> 00:31:29,762
to help the people in
the cooperative start over.

572
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:32,682
Ivy, how about Emilia?

573
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:35,643
What if she finds out you're doing this?

574
00:31:35,810 --> 00:31:39,188
Don't worry about Emilia.
Let me handle it.

575
00:31:40,523 --> 00:31:41,983
What's important is we help.

576
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:48,531
Look.

577
00:31:54,787 --> 00:31:57,790
[tense music playing]

578
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:11,387
Good morning.

579
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:12,639
Have some breakfast.

580
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:15,308
Good morning.

581
00:32:17,894 --> 00:32:22,106
The weather's nice today,
just like your mood.

582
00:32:22,565 --> 00:32:25,068
Of course! Why wouldn't I be?

583
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:27,278
I've fixed all our problems.

584
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:29,739
Except for one small thing.

585
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:33,201
You.

586
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:36,496
Do you think I forgot what you did to me?

587
00:32:36,579 --> 00:32:38,790
You didn't come home for our anniversary.

588
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:42,919
You know what? Starting today,
you're not allowed to go out.

589
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:45,254
And you'll stop that business of yours.

590
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:48,841
You can only go out
if my men will accompany you.

591
00:32:48,925 --> 00:32:51,761
You'll be with me, 24/7.

592
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:55,682
Wait, what is this?

593
00:32:55,765 --> 00:32:57,558
Am I in high school again?

594
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:59,769
Are you grounding me? Is that it?

595
00:32:59,852 --> 00:33:03,022
That, or I'll have you arrested
for what you did to Papa.

596
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:05,441
You decide.

597
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,000
[tense music playing]

598
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:23,960
<i>A story still came out.</i>

599
00:33:24,043 --> 00:33:26,796
<i>Fine. But you better be ready</i>
<i>for what I'll do next.</i>

600
00:33:30,216 --> 00:33:31,801
Just sit here, okay?

601
00:33:31,926 --> 00:33:34,595
I'll just get the clothes
I left outside to dry.

602
00:33:35,388 --> 00:33:36,389
Stay there.

603
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:41,936
[pensive music plays]

604
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:01,414
Jasmin.

605
00:34:13,801 --> 00:34:14,802
Jasmin?

606
00:34:25,938 --> 00:34:26,939
Diego.

607
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,280
Ivy, what are you doing here?

608
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:37,116
How are you?

609
00:34:40,369 --> 00:34:42,371
I mean, how's everyone?

610
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:48,961
I just want to know if you're
all okay after what happened.

611
00:34:52,673 --> 00:34:53,508
Uh…

612
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:01,808
Diego.

613
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:10,399
What's this for?

614
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:15,404
I want to help all the people here.

615
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:17,740
So the cooperative can start over.

616
00:35:22,745 --> 00:35:23,996
Thank you, Ivy, but…

617
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:26,791
we can't accept this.

618
00:35:28,167 --> 00:35:29,710
No, Diego. Please.

619
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:30,711
Please, accept it.

620
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:33,339
-I just want to help.
-No, we can't accept this.

621
00:35:33,422 --> 00:35:34,257
I just--

622
00:35:34,340 --> 00:35:36,092
I know this is the only way
you can help us now.

623
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:37,844
And I don't hold it against you.

624
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:48,938
It's easy to trade dignity for money.

625
00:35:50,606 --> 00:35:54,735
But money has always made things
worse for the people here.

626
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:58,489
Their dignity and principles
are all they have left…

627
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:03,452
and those are the things we'll
hold onto until the very end.

628
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:06,289
[tense music playing]

629
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:30,146
Looks like you're only waiting
for the party's endorsement

630
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:32,607
to push through with
your senatorial bid, Emilia.

631
00:36:33,149 --> 00:36:34,317
Talk is cheap, Senator.

632
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:36,319
So, when are we going to make it official?

633
00:36:36,777 --> 00:36:38,487
Well, at last,

634
00:36:38,571 --> 00:36:41,908
you had the guts to evict those farmers.

635
00:36:42,408 --> 00:36:44,785
That shows your strong conviction,

636
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:48,456
and I assume you'll fix
your problems with your son.

637
00:36:49,665 --> 00:36:51,125
I'll fix it all, Senator.

638
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:53,669
For as long as you continue to endorse me.

639
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:55,630
And I promise to give it my best.

640
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:57,798
I won't disappoint you, or the party.

641
00:36:58,549 --> 00:36:59,592
Shall we?

642
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:07,642
[townsfolk chanting] We will
fight for our land rights!

643
00:37:07,808 --> 00:37:09,602
We will fight for our land rights!

644
00:37:09,685 --> 00:37:12,063
You can't do that here, sir.
We don't want any trouble.

645
00:37:12,146 --> 00:37:13,898
[man] We just want to talk
to the governor.

646
00:37:13,981 --> 00:37:15,274
Governor, they've been there all day.

647
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:16,609
[man] We'll just talk to her.

648
00:37:16,692 --> 00:37:17,652
[guard] They don't want to leave.

649
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:18,527
[man] We'll fight for our…

650
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:20,613
-Should we make them leave?
-No, no, no, no.

651
00:37:20,696 --> 00:37:21,697
[townsfolk] Fight for our land rights!

652
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:24,784
A good leader knows how
to handle her detractors.

653
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:27,245
I'll face them. I'll fix this.

654
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:29,247
-All right, ma'am.
-Fight for our rights!

655
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:30,456
Mr. Fernan, the governor.

656
00:37:30,539 --> 00:37:32,250
[townsfolk chanting]
We'll fight for our land!

657
00:37:32,333 --> 00:37:34,377
-Fight!
-For our land!

658
00:37:34,460 --> 00:37:37,046
We will fight for our land rights!

659
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:39,548
We will fight for our land rights!

660
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,218
We will fight for our land rights!

661
00:37:42,301 --> 00:37:44,804
We will fight for our land rights!

662
00:37:44,929 --> 00:37:46,681
Governor, good afternoon.

663
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:50,017
Mr. Fernan, Mr. Ramon,
what brings you here?

664
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,686
Drop the act, Governor.

665
00:37:51,769 --> 00:37:54,689
We're here to fight for our land!

666
00:37:54,772 --> 00:37:55,690
[townsfolk] That's right!

667
00:37:55,773 --> 00:38:00,695
Mr. Ramon, we politicians know
what's best for you citizens.

668
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:03,531
But was it right to lock us up?

669
00:38:03,614 --> 00:38:04,782
To have us arrested?!

670
00:38:04,865 --> 00:38:06,284
To have your son beaten up?!

671
00:38:06,367 --> 00:38:07,702
-That's right!
-That's right!

672
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:10,913
Mr. Ramon, aren't you
Mr. Fernan's right-hand man?

673
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:14,959
When the EPZ project begins,
I'll make you the head.

674
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,169
We don't need that!

675
00:38:17,253 --> 00:38:20,715
What we need
is the ownership of that land!

676
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:23,301
-That's right!
-If you don't give it back,

677
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:27,722
I will bring this issue to
your political enemies myself!

678
00:38:27,805 --> 00:38:29,724
-What?
-So that no Ardiente will win

679
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:31,892
-in the next election!
-That's right!

680
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:34,228
We have the right to go
against the Ardientes!

681
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,397
Our rights against the Ardientes!

682
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:38,190
Freedom from the Ardientes!

683
00:38:38,274 --> 00:38:40,568
Freedom from the Ardientes!

684
00:38:40,651 --> 00:38:42,611
We will fight for our land rights!

685
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:44,864
We will fight for our land rights!

686
00:38:44,947 --> 00:38:47,616
We will fight for our land rights!

687
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:49,702
We will fight for our land rights!

688
00:38:49,785 --> 00:38:52,163
We will fight for our land rights!

689
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:55,541
[tense music playing]

690
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:02,882
-<i>You!</i>
-[Emilia cries]

691
00:39:02,965 --> 00:39:06,802
<i>You and your weaknesses as a woman!</i>

692
00:39:16,062 --> 00:39:17,396
<i>-You never think, do you?</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

693
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:20,691
<i>A woman like you, getting</i>
<i>herself drunk senseless?!</i>

694
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:22,526
<i>-Have some dignity!</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

695
00:39:23,152 --> 00:39:23,986
<i>Ouch!</i>

696
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:27,615
<i>I don't want you to be involved</i>
<i>in any of this anymore.</i>

697
00:39:28,657 --> 00:39:30,576
<i>Emilia, you disappoint me.</i>

698
00:39:31,285 --> 00:39:32,828
<i>-I meant--</i>
<i>-Shut up.</i>

699
00:39:32,912 --> 00:39:34,914
<i>Let the men handle this.</i>

700
00:39:34,997 --> 00:39:37,666
<i>A woman like you wouldn't</i>
<i>understand anything.</i>

701
00:39:37,750 --> 00:39:39,502
<i>There are things about your credentials</i>

702
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:40,920
<i>which we find lacking.</i>

703
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:43,714
<i>If you can't reach Julio's</i>
<i>level of influence,</i>

704
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:45,716
<i>you'll only be wasting time and money.</i>

705
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,385
<i>Because you'll surely lose.</i>

706
00:39:48,344 --> 00:39:49,845
<i>I'll fix it all, Senator.</i>

707
00:39:49,929 --> 00:39:52,723
<i>For as long as you continue to endorse me.</i>

708
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:54,433
<i>And I promise to give it my best.</i>

709
00:39:54,517 --> 00:39:56,310
<i>I won't disappoint you, or the party.</i>

710
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:59,688
<i>What we need is the ownership</i>
<i>of that land!</i>

711
00:39:59,772 --> 00:40:03,192
<i>If you won't give it to us,</i>
<i>I will bring this issue…</i>

712
00:40:03,275 --> 00:40:04,693
<i>to your political enemies myself!</i>

713
00:40:04,777 --> 00:40:06,362
<i>-What?</i>
<i>-So that no Ardiente…</i>

714
00:40:06,445 --> 00:40:08,781
<i>-will win in the next election!</i>
<i>-That's right!</i>

715
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:13,452
[tense music intensifies]

716
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:19,834
[line ringing]

717
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:21,794
Hello.

718
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:25,297
[tense music playing]

719
00:40:27,925 --> 00:40:29,760
-There.
-I warned you, Ramon.

720
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:32,388
You shouldn't have argued
with the governor like that!

721
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:34,723
You know how Mr. Ramon is, Dad.

722
00:40:34,807 --> 00:40:36,809
He blows up once he's fed up.

723
00:40:37,309 --> 00:40:39,895
I used to fight for the Ardientes

724
00:40:39,979 --> 00:40:41,689
and defended them
against their detractors.

725
00:40:41,772 --> 00:40:42,773
Oh, come on.

726
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:45,317
But this time, they've crossed the line!

727
00:40:46,610 --> 00:40:47,945
What's your plan, Mr. Ramon?

728
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:49,864
Are you pushing through with your threat?

729
00:40:51,782 --> 00:40:54,910
If the governor won't stop
trying to steal our land.

730
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:56,787
Okay. That's enough.

731
00:40:56,871 --> 00:40:58,164
Let's just finish this.

732
00:40:58,789 --> 00:40:59,748
-Jack.
-Yes?

733
00:40:59,832 --> 00:41:02,168
-Isn't that ready yet?
-Everything's all tapped.

734
00:41:02,251 --> 00:41:04,295
-But still no power.
-Good grief.

735
00:41:04,378 --> 00:41:05,838
Just a bit more, and we'll be done here.

736
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:07,715
All right then.

737
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:09,508
I'll go check the power lines.

738
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:11,760
I think I saw
a loose cable there last night.

739
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:12,845
-All right.
-You stay here.

740
00:41:12,928 --> 00:41:14,013
All right. Take care, okay?

741
00:41:14,096 --> 00:41:15,598
Wrap that around there. Right there.

742
00:41:15,681 --> 00:41:16,849
It might fall over.

743
00:41:17,558 --> 00:41:18,809
Where's Loring?

744
00:41:20,269 --> 00:41:21,395
I'm getting hungry.

745
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:27,735
[ominous music playing]

746
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:44,543
I heard the news.

747
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:48,297
I must admit, I'm surprised
you could do that.

748
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:52,259
I'm surprised you could do that to me.

749
00:41:53,928 --> 00:41:56,013
You had me beaten up by your private army.

750
00:41:57,806 --> 00:42:00,434
I know we disagree
on a lot of things, but…

751
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:03,771
but I can't believe
that just because of this…

752
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:06,774
you turned your back on your own brother.

753
00:42:06,857 --> 00:42:09,360
You can't quit being stupid, can you?

754
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:11,070
Why don't you tell yourself
the same thing?

755
00:42:11,153 --> 00:42:13,113
You're the one who turned
your back on this family!

756
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:15,699
Don't you dare think that
I'll just let this slide.

757
00:42:16,867 --> 00:42:19,119
I'm not the kid you used to make fun of.

758
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:21,747
Whatever you do to me…

759
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:24,041
I can do to you, too.

760
00:42:24,917 --> 00:42:27,962
[tense music playing]

761
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,725
-It's delicious.
-Here you go.

762
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:42,726
Can I have some?

763
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,645
-Where's Ramon?
-Me, too.

764
00:42:44,728 --> 00:42:45,813
Hold on.

765
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:47,690
Ramon's not here yet.

766
00:42:47,773 --> 00:42:49,441
Nimfa, why don't you bring him some?

767
00:42:49,525 --> 00:42:51,694
-Hey, save some for me.
-We will. Don't worry.

768
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:53,779
-We'll save you some.
-We can't finish all of this.

769
00:42:54,822 --> 00:42:55,990
[Nimfa] Mr. Ramon!

770
00:42:56,782 --> 00:42:59,785
Time to eat! Miss Loring
prepared some food for us.

771
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:03,872
Mr. Ramon?

772
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:06,417
[ominous music playing]

773
00:43:21,557 --> 00:43:22,891
Mr. Ramon!

774
00:43:22,975 --> 00:43:24,059
Help!

775
00:43:24,143 --> 00:43:25,269
Please, help me!

776
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:27,855
[muffled] Help! Help--

777
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:30,566
Mister, help us!

778
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:33,777
[tense music playing]

779
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:35,404
Mister.

780
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:41,201
[gasps]

781
00:43:44,163 --> 00:43:45,706
[indistinct chatter]

782
00:43:45,789 --> 00:43:47,124
[Diego] Hey, everyone!

783
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:50,878
-Let's eat up!
-[cheering]

784
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:54,715
Oh, my. What did you bring?

785
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:57,968
-Noodles, Nanny.
-Oh, wow.

786
00:43:58,052 --> 00:44:00,346
You just had to compete
with me, didn't you?

787
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:01,722
-Let me get that for you.
-Nanny…

788
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:06,477
your cooking is still
the best here in the whole town.

789
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:08,687
-Isn't that right, everyone?
-That's right!

790
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:11,690
-Long live Loring!
-This is still the best.

791
00:44:11,774 --> 00:44:13,692
Oh, really now? All right.
Let's open this up.

792
00:44:13,776 --> 00:44:15,444
Let's dig in!

793
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:18,030
Looks good!

794
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:19,782
[Loring] What do you want?

795
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:21,033
-Let's eat!
-I want some.

796
00:44:22,534 --> 00:44:23,661
What?

797
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:25,120
[Dolfo] It's so sad to think…

798
00:44:25,829 --> 00:44:28,624
our days here at the co-op are numbered.

799
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:31,543
Come on, Rodolfo, don't think like that.

800
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:36,924
Especially now that your son,
Ramon, and Fernan

801
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:39,176
have joined forces,
we're stronger than ever!

802
00:44:39,259 --> 00:44:40,678
-Really?
-That's right.

803
00:44:40,761 --> 00:44:43,847
And while we live, there's hope.

804
00:44:43,931 --> 00:44:45,641
-That's right.
-I agree.

805
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:48,519
All we have to do is to fight fair.

806
00:44:48,602 --> 00:44:50,521
-Correct.
-That's right.

807
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:52,815
Just like Diego here.

808
00:44:52,898 --> 00:44:55,692
Diego, thank you for standing up for us.

809
00:44:55,776 --> 00:44:58,237
You're so kind and brave.

810
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:00,489
-[man] You're our idol.
-Of course, Nanny.

811
00:45:00,781 --> 00:45:02,533
Just keep giving me fritters,
and I'll be fine.

812
00:45:02,616 --> 00:45:04,993
-Wow.
-Here's the noodles.

813
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:07,663
-Time for the noodles.
-Noodles for long life.

814
00:45:08,705 --> 00:45:10,791
I brought a lot of noodles.

815
00:45:11,542 --> 00:45:13,752
-Nimfa! Over here!
-[Nimfa cries]

816
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:16,797
-[Loring] This is for long life.
-[indistinct chatter]

817
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,674
-Nimfa.
-Hey, Nimfa. Are you okay?

818
00:45:18,757 --> 00:45:19,800
[Loring] What happened?

819
00:45:20,801 --> 00:45:21,802
Mr. Dolfo.

820
00:45:23,178 --> 00:45:24,555
-What is it?
-It's…

821
00:45:24,930 --> 00:45:27,349
it's about Mr. Ramon.

822
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:28,934
What happened to my son?

823
00:45:29,685 --> 00:45:31,019
Where's Ramon? What happened to him?

824
00:45:34,773 --> 00:45:36,066
-Hey.
-Nimfa.

825
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:38,444
Nimfa, what happened to Mr. Ramon?

826
00:45:39,778 --> 00:45:40,654
Nimfa.

827
00:45:41,738 --> 00:45:42,739
Nimfa.

828
00:45:44,450 --> 00:45:46,034
Mr. Ramon got into an accident.

829
00:45:49,538 --> 00:45:52,166
-What happened?
-Mr. Dolfo.

830
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:57,546
-Ramon, my son!
-[townsfolk crying]

831
00:45:58,130 --> 00:45:59,339
[man] What happened to Ramon?

832
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:01,592
Ramon! My son!

833
00:46:04,928 --> 00:46:06,555
-Mr. Dolfo.
-Dolfo.

834
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:08,557
- Ramon, my son!
-Dolfo. Dolfo.

835
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:10,726
[Loring] Why Ramon?

836
00:46:10,809 --> 00:46:12,269
He was still so young.

837
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:13,562
Why did this happen to him?

838
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:16,190
Why is this happening to us?

839
00:46:16,273 --> 00:46:18,734
If that's what Ramon's fate is--

840
00:46:18,817 --> 00:46:20,360
[Diego] Uncle Pandoy's right.

841
00:46:20,903 --> 00:46:22,404
It was an accident.

842
00:46:23,363 --> 00:46:25,574
No, Diego.

843
00:46:25,657 --> 00:46:28,452
This wasn't an accident.

844
00:46:31,580 --> 00:46:34,625
I saw someone following Mr. Ramon…

845
00:46:35,501 --> 00:46:38,754
but when I got there, he ran off.

846
00:46:39,922 --> 00:46:42,049
This wasn't an accident.

847
00:46:42,132 --> 00:46:44,384
Are you saying somebody killed
Mister Ramon?

848
00:46:47,387 --> 00:46:50,432
-Governor.
-Yes? What's the problem?

849
00:46:50,516 --> 00:46:51,808
Nothing big, Governor.

850
00:46:52,184 --> 00:46:53,727
If they're not suspecting anything

851
00:46:53,810 --> 00:46:56,772
after I had Ramon killed,
then why do we have to talk?

852
00:46:56,855 --> 00:46:58,357
The thing is, Governor…

853
00:46:58,774 --> 00:47:00,651
Mr. Fernan's daughter saw me.

854
00:47:01,276 --> 00:47:02,402
What?!

855
00:47:02,569 --> 00:47:04,196
Do you think this is connected

856
00:47:04,279 --> 00:47:07,199
to Ramon's threat against the governor?

857
00:47:08,534 --> 00:47:10,786
What do you mean, Mr. Dolfo?

858
00:47:11,453 --> 00:47:13,622
But I'm sure she didn't recognize me.

859
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:17,042
Well, we can't do anything
about the mess you made.

860
00:47:17,918 --> 00:47:19,795
But it's good that happened.

861
00:47:19,962 --> 00:47:22,005
So they start to realize

862
00:47:22,089 --> 00:47:24,800
that they shouldn't be going
against the Ardientes.

863
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:32,099
[dramatic music playing]

864
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:39,481
[screams]

865
00:47:55,789 --> 00:47:57,040
[Arnaldo] <i>You always make decisions</i>

866
00:47:57,124 --> 00:47:58,917
<i>without thinking of the consequences.</i>

867
00:47:59,001 --> 00:48:00,711
[Emilia] <i>You think you're better than me?</i>

868
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:02,296
<i>I wish I wasn't born an Ardiente!</i>

869
00:48:02,379 --> 00:48:03,338
[Ivy] <i>I'm really sorry.</i>

870
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:05,716
<i>I just came here to offer my condolences</i>

871
00:48:05,799 --> 00:48:08,635
<i>and tell you that the project is on hold.</i>

872
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:10,137
<i>Did someone have to die first</i>

873
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:12,014
<i>before you realized</i>
<i>what you're doing is wrong?</i>

874
00:48:12,097 --> 00:48:14,891
[Jepoy] <i>Mayor, I heard Miss</i>
<i>Aguas was going to the co-op.</i>

875
00:48:14,975 --> 00:48:16,101
<i>Why would she go there?</i>

876
00:48:16,184 --> 00:48:18,478
<i>She knows the farmers</i>
<i>have a rift with the Ardientes!</i>

877
00:48:19,229 --> 00:48:21,106
<i>-Ivy, wait.</i>
<i>-You're concerned?</i>

878
00:48:21,189 --> 00:48:23,817
<i>Do you think I'd ever let you get hurt?</i>

879
00:48:28,488 --> 00:48:30,490
[theme music plays]
